__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Client data: belt and braces -------------------------------------
# scripts/scrub_check.py already BLOCKS a commit containing any of these.
# This list is the second layer, so they never reach the index at all —
# a .gitignore is not a substitute for the gate (it is trivially bypassed
# with `git add -f`, and it does nothing about what is already tracked),
# but between the two, an accident has to defeat both.
#
# The reason this matters more than usual: a run writes deed PDFs, page
# images, a report, a result JSON and a run log into its output folder,
# and if that folder is ever pointed at a checkout, every one of those
# files is a recorded instrument tied to a named person and address.
*.pdf
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.docx
* - result.json
*result.*.json
# A rule-inventory snapshot quotes SKILL.md verbatim; taken from the
# private working copy it carries the client names in the guardrail prose.
*.rules.json
legal_description_run_log.json
run_log*
registry_profile.json

# Never, under any circumstances, the pseudonymization map or the tools
# that carry the real names. They live OUTSIDE this repository by design.
*namemap*
*apply_scrub*
*verify_scrub*
*scrub_inventory*
*PRIVATE*

# Credentials and local environments
.env
*.pem
*.key
.venv/
venv/
